      "body": "Ignore `.monarch/` (Monarch's job API writes `.monarch/job_state.pkl` and its logs into the launch directory) and `/structured_logs/` (written there when the dump folder is the repo root). Both have been committed by accident, and a committed `job_state.pkl` can break the next launch from a checkout of that commit.\n\nNOTE: prevention only. Upstream launchers don't use Monarch's job API, and the default dump folder (`outputs/rl`) is already ignored.\n\n**Test plan**\n```\n$ git check-ignore -v .monarch/job_state.pkl structured_logs/x.jsonl\n.gitignore:56:.monarch/\t.monarch/job_state.pkl\n.gitignore:57:/structured_logs/\tstructured_logs/x.jsonl\n```\nOn main the same command prints nothing (exit 1). A nested `torchtitan/rl/structured_logs/y.jsonl` stays unignored: the pattern is anchored to the repo root.\n",
